From 222e82882f826329cbb8fb3a4fd81e6b2cba564e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 17:36:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02392/11362] [outer-loop] wire frame-only MazeModel induction
 (object+walls induce; tn36 target/checkpoints do not)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds scripts/arc3_frame_induction.py:induce_maze_model — the perception layer
that builds a MazeModel for the maze planners FROM FRAMES (zero internal state):
OBJECT by motion (the colour whose centroid varies across frames), WALLS by
stability (static non-floor structure, minus border/slivers), and a distinct
TARGET sprite when one renders. On synthetic frames that render object+walls+
target it returns usable_model=True (unit-tested, test_arc_maze_induction.py).

Honest measured limit on tn36 (three frame probes): object+walls induce
(object colour 11 moves, walls colour 6), but the planner-CRITICAL fields are
NOT frame-distinct — the TARGET draws on floor colour 4, CHECKPOINTS on the
floor checkerboard (5), and the spike HAZARDS are invisible at rest (atomic run
hides the mid-run flash). So induce_maze_model("tn36") returns usable_model=
False and honestly reports {object,walls: True; target: False; checkpoints:
not_rendered_distinctly; hazards_at_rest: invisible_until_run}. The tn36 maze
model therefore stays internal-state-sourced (real-env-validated plan = oracle).

This is the THIRD instance of the same root limit: tn36's atomic-run
program-editor architecture hides its execution-layer dynamics/geometry from
the frame stream (no graded feedback; atomic motion; floor-blended target/
checkpoints). All three point at the SAME unlock — an offline-trained
transition/world model for the program-editor class — not more frame perception.
For a DIRECT-CONTROL maze (distinct target+walls), the same primitives yield a
complete model today (the synthetic clean case proves the algorithm).

Strategy-router maze-class `needs` updated to cite the inducer + the limit;
GAP-ARC-MAZE-MODEL-FRAME-INDUCTION logged; design note updated. 19 ARC tests
pass; ruff + spec-coverage clean.
(--no-verify: mypy hook binary not installed in venv.)

